      "slug": "magic-ring-a74",
      "term": "Magic ring",
      "definition": "An adjustable loop used to start crocheting in the round. Pull the tail to close the centre hole after working the first round."
    },
    {
      "slug": "invisible-decrease-a74",
      "term": "Invisible decrease",
      "definition": "A dc2tog through the front loops only of two consecutive stitches. Produces a neater surface than a standard decrease."
    },
    {
      "slug": "fringe-trim-a74",
      "term": "Fringe trim",
      "definition": "Short lengths of yarn knotted through a row of stitches to create a decorative fringe. For the fairy's skirt, loop short pieces of sparkle or contrast yarn through the stitches at the lower body to suggest a layered skirt."
    }
